[] Killed some hill orcs. Finally got to 'em, dropped 'em
[] on Omikami-san's altar.  Too late. "Nothing happens."
[] Fine.  Find a brand-new orc, slice 'im up, immediately
[] pick him up and drop him on the altar, two steps away.
[] Nothing happens.  That's because he was lumped in with the
[] old orcs.  This has happened before; you always have to 
[] remove the older carcasses if you want to sacrifice a 
[] new one, or else risk losing it.
[]
[] Oh, Nethack 3.0, patchlevel 9

yeah, this is a special case and should probably get special treatment.

what normally happens with corpses is that a new corpse "averages" the
age of the already lumped corpses (i.e. the lumped corpses get younger
and the new corpse ages a lot).  you can get strange results like finding
that your pile of "nothing happens" corpses suddenly becomes "active"
with the addition of a new corpse!

there's a related bug: you can't normally sacrifice zombie-like corpses
since they are already old.  however, if you attempt to eat the corpse
and get interrupted then you can sacrifice the partly eaten corpse.  of
course, attempting to eat old corpses has its own risks ...

